# SHA-256 of workshop/site/hackathon.html: the freeze baseline for AC21 (specs/005-teaching-spa.md).
# The page stays byte-identical until workshop/spa/docs/hackathon-retired.md exists. A rehearsal
# record, passing or failing, does not release it.
#
# The digest is of the exact bytes of the file on disk; tests/spa/hackathon-untouched.test.ts
# hashes it as read, with no line-ending normalization. It was taken in the freeze worktree, where
# the page is the CRLF checkout that git for Windows makes under its system gitconfig
# (core.autocrlf=true): 203350 bytes, all 3581 line endings CRLF. To reproduce:
#   PowerShell: (Get-FileHash -Algorithm SHA256 workshop/site/hackathon.html).Hash
#   POSIX:      sha256sum workshop/site/hackathon.html
#
# Environment limit: git stores the page with LF endings (199769 bytes, SHA-256
# 0fc164d64b5f03ccb76256f876641026297a35c14e10c6c73b15a74aea9a61cb). A checkout that does not
# convert line endings, such as Linux CI, holds those bytes instead and fails the guard against
# the digest below. Do not edit the digest to make one checkout pass: the cause is that the
# page's line endings are not pinned. Pinning them (a .gitattributes rule for this one path) is
# outside child issue 12; when it lands, record the digest of the pinned form.
343e783eb0252d984a474010c3a90d83c16f3f3d8591951cef2fd5fd9770edf2
